Prove that the orthocenter of the triangle formed by the three lines $y = m_1x + alm_1, y = m_2x
+ alm_2, y = m_3x + alm_3$ is $\left[-a, \left(\frac{1}{m_1} + \frac{1}{m_2} + \frac{1}{m_3}
+ \frac{1}{m_1m_2m_3}\right)\right]$.


Prove that the diagonals of the parallelogram formed by the lines $\frac{x}{a} + \frac{y}{b} = 1,
\frac{x}{b} + \frac{y}{a} = 1, \frac{x}{a} + \frac{y}{b} = 2$ and $\frac{x}{b} + \frac{y}{a}
= 2$ are at right angles.
